      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e `PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL` is required for ps8815 firmware update.\n\u003e if a platform does not use a ps8xxx TCPC, there probably is no other\n\u003e dependency that would call for enabling this. \n\u003e \n\u003e `PLATFORM_EC_CONSOLE_CMD_I2C_SPEED` is optional.\n\u003e it is mainly used to test different I2C speeds and was helpful\n\u003e in debugging the ps8xxx firmware updater.\n\nThanks Caveh for the suggestion, \n\neven with https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3930043 CL, I\u0027m running into `ps8815.1: Could not set I2C bus speed to 400 kHz!` issue.",
      "parentUuid": "5b3121fb_df3ca89a",
      "revId": "04446684ceac77e61b9017bb442c57b6db5b9b05",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
